    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, led by **Yordan Alvarez**, who anchors the lineup with a robust 79.62 score. Despite facing a mid-tier matchup against Luis Castillo, **Yordan Alvarez**\u2019s elite .451 xwOBA and prime #2 spot in the order make him our most reliable ceiling play. Following closely is **Junior Caminero** (72.80), whose prime positioning at #3 against Cal Quantrill provides a significant volume boost. We are also leaning into speed today, as **Caleb Durbin** (70.78) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (68.67) both benefit from favorable stolen base environments against pitchers with slower deliveries, a critical factor given our league's scarcity-driven focus on SB categories.\n\nWe are actively exploiting platoon advantages to maximize daily efficiency, most notably with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.03), whose 14% dynamic platoon boost mitigates the difficulty of facing Logan Henderson. Similarly, **Josh Smith** (61.73) and **Christian Yelich** (61.36) are both strong starts, bolstered by high-upside platoon splits that elevate them above the marginal tier. The most difficult decision at the margins was passing over **Pedro Ramirez** (37.39). While **Pedro Ramirez** holds some utility as a switch-hitter, his projected #7 spot in the lineup and the suboptimal matchup against Henderson kept him below our start-worthy threshold.\n\nStrategic caution is advised regarding **Gary Sanchez** and **Jacob Gonzalez**, both of whom are currently hovering in the \"Marginal\" 40\u201350 range. **Gary Sanchez** is facing the high-strikeout arm of Kevin Gausman, and his score is depressed by a poor BvP history and a lack of confirmed lineup placement. While **Jacob Gonzalez** maintains a decent floor, he is anchored by a bottom-of-the-order assignment that limits his plate appearance upside. We will be monitoring lineups closely for **Gary Sanchez**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Junior Caminero** to ensure that our projected efficiency holds as managers finalize their cards.",
